      <p>With 82.3% of winning composers taking the prize exactly once, the Best Original Score Oscar has
      historically functioned as a broad acknowledgment of excellence rather than a vehicle for building
      repeat dynasties. Even the top winners — Barry, Williams, Göransson — cap out at 4 wins across
